{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["From Kivrot HaTa'ava the people journeyed to Hazerot — by the plain sense: from Kivrot HaTa'ava the people journeyed to Hazerot, and they were there in Hazerot, meaning, they tarried there until Miriam's re-gathering. And therefore he lengthened his expression: ויהיו בחצרות. And the derash of Aggadah in the Sifrei at the end of the parasha: ואחר נסעו העם מחצרות ויחנו במדבר פארן — were there then two Hazerot, that they journeyed from this one and encamped in that one, and journeyed from that one and encamped in this one?! And this was doubtful to my teachers and I was asked about it in Paris and I explained it in a derasha: for this latter we learn from the beginning of the parasha, where it is written: מקברות התאוה נסעו העם חצרות ויהיו בחצרות — and on this verse the Sifrei writes: this was at the hour when Miriam was stricken with tzara'at; and the end of the matter returns and concludes it with the last verse of the parasha: ואחר נסעו העם מחצרות — were there then two Hazerot, etc. And this latter verse is expounded as: מקברות התאוה נסעו העם ויחנו בחצרות, like all the other journeys and encampments where ויסעו ויחנו is written. Rather, מקברות התאוה נסעו העם חצרות — it implies that the people journeyed from Hazerot and afterward ויהיו בחצרות, that they turned back to behind them, to Hazerot: for when the first standard journeyed from Hazerot and the Mishkan had not yet been taken down [and the Levites had not journeyed], and Moshe and Aharon and Miriam, who were still in the camp of Leviyya — the Holy One, blessed be He, suddenly called to them, and Miriam was stricken with tzara'at, and they turned back to behind them, and Miriam was re-gathered from her tzara'at at the conclusion of seven days, ואחר נסעו העם מחצרות ויחנו במדבר פארן. And I found this entire derasha in the Mekhilta in Parashat Beshalach, all in the first verse. And I also found it in the responsa of R. Kalonymos of Rome, like myself. And also what is written in the Mekhilta: ויסעו בני ישראל מרעמס סכתה — on this it is said: ואשא אתכם על כנפי נשרים — and I explained to those who asked: because there it is not written ויסעו מרעמסס ויחנו סכתה. This tells you that temporarily they came from Ra'amses to Sukkot, and at the hour they journeyed from Ra'amses they journeyed as well from Sukkot, and this is כנפי נשרים."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Rashbam appears to quote the Mekhilta's paraphrase of Exodus 12:37 rather than the exact biblical text; rendered as he writes it. The parenthetical 'and the Levites had not journeyed' appears in brackets in the source, suggesting a marginal or variant insertion; translated as part of the comment."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:50:08.187743994Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}